    "status": "present",
    "value": "After each incoming character, decide whether any stored dictionary word is a suffix of the stream seen so far. The approach is: reversed-word trie checks suffixes in a bounded recent-character buffer. Its target cost is build O(total word length); query O(max word length); bounded stream storage. Treat the invariant underlying that approach as the reason each local update preserves the required result. Check it against an independent bounded reference before relying on large-domain constructions."
  },
